 "description": "Connect a social account. Opens the platform in the person's browser so they can sign in and approve access \u2014 that part cannot happen here, because it needs their session and their consent. Call it again after they finish and it reports the connected account.\n\nWith `invite`, the link is for someone else instead \u2014 a friend or family member who will create a brand-new account and connect it, with no login of their own here. They get a page showing the profile to set up (picture, username, name, bio) with copy buttons, the steps to switch Instagram to a Creator account, and a Connect button. Give the person the `url`. Calling again with the same platform and username returns the same invite, updated with whatever profile fields are given, and its status \u2014 so that is also how to check whether they have finished. Upload the profile picture first with media_upload and media_confirm, and pass its id.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "properties": {
   "invite": {
    "description": "Set to make a link for someone without a login here, who will create the account. Leave out to connect an account yourself.",
    "properties": {
     "avatar_media_id": {
      "description": "An image from media_upload/media_confirm to use as the profile picture. The invite goes into the same workspace as the image.",
      "type": "string"
     },
     "bio": {
      "description": "The profile bio. Instagram caps it at 150 characters.",
      "maxLength": 150,
      "type": "string"
     },
     "display_name": {
      "description": "The profile name shown above the bio.",
      "maxLength": 64,
      "type": "string"
     },
     "username": {
      "description": "The handle they should register, without the @. Also what identifies this invite on a repeat call. Instagram allows letters, numbers, periods and underscores, up to 30.",
      "maxLength": 31,
      "minLength": 1,
      "type": "string"
     }
    },
    "required": [
     "username"
    ],
    "type": "object"
   },
   "platform": {
    "description": "Which platform to connect.",
    "enum": [
     "tiktok",
     "instagram",
     "facebook",
     "youtube",
     "x"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "platform"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
